{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0198wU3jVnWfMYNfLMD6YAdL","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"c2d4b9fc2937b12a5dcf09d55d509c3a4abfac77\",\"date\":\"2026-09-22T23:35:08+08:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5997: Make service queues metric values less shouty (#2766)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) O3-5997: Make service queues metric values less shouty\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5997: Unbold the metric tile header labels\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5997: Match the header label style used in the other metrics strip\",\"authorName\":\"Ujjawal Prabhat\",\"authorEmail\":\"UjjawalPrabhat1@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"7dc40adfde68677979aa9422d5d00858a8213121\",\"date\":\"2026-09-22T20:54:37+05:30\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5983: Add the actions menu back to in-service patient cards (#2752)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) O3-5983: Add the actions menu back to in-service patient cards\\n\\nThe in-service cards on the queue page replaced the table rows that carried\\nthe Move, Edit, Remove patient and Undo transition actions, so those actions\\nwere lost.\\n\\nEach card now has an overflow menu in its top-right corner with those four\\nactions, reusing the queue table's action menu items so the handlers, labels\\nand visibility rules stay in one place. The menu sits outside the patient\\nchart link so opening it does not navigate away.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5983: Render queue actions as direct menu items and move the card menu beside the link\\n\\nCarbon's OverflowMenu clones each direct child with the ref and focus handlers its keyboard navigation relies on. The shared wrapper component dropped them, so arrow keys did not move between items in the card menu or the queue table. Replace the wrapper with a hook that returns the visible OverflowMenuItems directly.\\n\\nMark the shared remove action as a delete action to match its danger confirmation button.\\n\\nPlace the card's actions menu beside the patient chart link instead of over it, so the two hit areas do not overlap. The service row extends under the menu column so its divider still reaches the card edge.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5983: Move the card actions menu into the queue status bar, outside the patient chart link\",\"authorName\":\"Nethmi Rodrigo\",\"authorEmail\":\"nethmi@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"71b3d3f10534189eafd4786628aeceecdb4a84c2\",\"date\":\"2026-09-21T22:24:56+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) O3-5924: Use React-scoped JSX types (#2763)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Replace global JSX.Element references with React.JSX.Element in registration, service queues and the admission workspace.\\n\\nPrepare for React 19 types without changing the React 18 runtime or JSX build configuration.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"d6ca1f1c04e431bcaa7c79d46fd9027639db49eb\",\"date\":\"2026-09-21T18:04:19+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Adopt the shared Prettier configuration (#2764)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* chore: Adopt the shared Prettier configuration\\n\\nUse @openmrs/prettier-config in the existing config wrapper and pin Prettier to 3.9.8. Keep our bracketSameLine override.\\n\\n* Apply Prettier 3.9.8 formatting\\n\\nApply the measured indentation change in the service queues config schema. Leave existing formatting issues elsewhere untouched.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"c741c18000e41edbaefa3266b184c26507835735\",\"date\":\"2026-09-18T16:31:14-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2760)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"4f6944cc87106a2c5a59558189084d1dde29c2f2\",\"date\":\"2026-09-17T16:33:29-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2755)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"d9cbd2742a8d8842f6c7ae4d243254f195c06bd7\",\"date\":\"2026-09-17T22:12:04+05:30\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5984: Label in-service patients with the configured status name (#2750)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) O3-5984: Label in-service patients with the configured status name\\n\\nThe queue page's metric tile takes its label from the queue status concept\\n(\\\"In Service\\\"), while the card list above the tables used a fixed\\n\\\"Attending\\\" string, so the two disagreed. Derive the card heading, its error\\nstate title, and the clinic overview's column and totals card from the\\nconfigured defaultTransitionStatus concept instead, falling back to\\n\\\"In Service\\\" until the concept loads.\\n\\n* Update packages/esm-service-queues-app/src/attending-patients/attending-patients.test.tsx\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Nethmi Rodrigo\",\"authorEmail\":\"nethmi@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"1f4098170806704451ed195a9922dc1a30ebcedc\",\"date\":\"2026-09-14T20:01:27+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5958: Default the queue location to the one selected in Service Queues (#2731)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* fix(service-queues): ensure queueLocation defaults to sessionLocation asynchronously\\n\\n* fix(queue-fields): prefill queue location from service queues store with fallback to session location\\n\\n* fix(queue-fields): prefill queue location from service queues store with fallback to session location\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi@openmrs.org>\",\"authorName\":\"Mutagubya Jonathan\",\"authorEmail\":\"mutajonathan4@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"2824b5ebeda2fb6f7f6f47bf0db6dcf7dc47007d\",\"date\":\"2026-09-15T00:33:12+08:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-5967: Show the queue number instead of the status in the default queue table (#2738)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ujjawal Prabhat\",\"authorEmail\":\"UjjawalPrabhat1@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"9a3d0e504d8