{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QRbcU1bCk1QkNcyBtrYExR","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"b46bb56449a768d9ffb652006aa5eea2a8960c08\",\"date\":\"2026-08-28T18:08:33-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2705)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"f4163794c31570904d1b77259cfadd135136fb91\",\"date\":\"2026-08-28T22:58:50+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Clean build outputs before bundle size comparison (#2704)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"7212897e35ee9efa79192770f019651dcbd66cc1\",\"date\":\"2026-08-28T18:42:34+08:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-5763: Unify the Current visit and Previous visit views (#2600)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) O3-5763: Unify the Current visit and Previous visit views\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5763: Address review feedback on unified visit summary\\n\\n* (fix) Restore visit note authoring on the Current visit tab\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5763: Fix obs group crash, encounter editing and expanded row styles\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5763: Fix the e2e specs covering the unified visit summary\\n\\nServe the patient notes app in the e2e frontend, scope the encounter assertions\\nto the expanded row's table, and revalidate queue entries once per submit rather\\nthan twice.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5763: Analyze the e2e database before running the specs\\n\\nThe seeded image reports zero rows for every table, so MariaDB plans the queue\\nentry query, whose join spans ~44 tables, from full scans. That is harmless while\\nqueue_entry is empty and takes minutes once a spec inserts a row, hanging\\nservice-queues.spec.ts. Analyzing the schema takes under a second.\\n\\nAlso adds the mutate mock that usePastVisits now returns to the PastVisit tests.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5763: Address review feedback on the unified visit summary\\n\\nMoves the queue spec's API setup into e2e/commands so other queue specs can reuse\\nit, guards its teardown against a partial setup, and scopes the encounter locator\\nto the table. Also guards the edit handler against an unresolved patient, restores\\nthe date validity check, widens the form entry window to match the chart, and\\ncovers the past visit filter and the slot state in tests.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5763: Hand the visit summary our mutate for encounter deletes\\n\\nDeleting an encounter opens a modal rather than a workspace, so the workspace\\nsubscription never fires and both tabs kept showing the deleted encounter.\\nPairs with the chart accepting mutateVisitContext alongside onEditEncounter.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5763: Wait for the patient before mounting the vitals extension\\n\\nThe vitals extension reads  during render — with a nonzero\\nbmiMinimumAge, shouldShowBmi reaches patient.birthDate before the extension's\\nown loading guard — so mounting it while usePatient is still resolving throws\\ninto the error boundary. Extends the existing patient-loading test to cover it.\\n\\n* (chore) O3-5763: Drop the CI database statistics workaround\\n\\nThe queue entry list was slow because the module fetched its associations\\neagerly, not because of the image. Fixed properly in openmrs-module-queue#122,\\nso this step comes out.\\n\\n* (feat) O3-5763: Hand the patient down to the visit summary extension\\n\\nThe shared visit summary reads the patient from the chart store, which Service\\nQueues never populates, so its embedded form view had nothing to render with.\\nBoth tabs now pass `patient` in the slot state, and the slot assertions cover\\n`patient`, `onEditEncounter` and `mutateVisitContext` so dropping one is caught\\nhere rather than in the e2e run.\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: jwnasambu <33891016+jwnasambu@users.noreply.github.com>\\nCo-authored-by: Ujjawal Prabhat <ujjawal@Ujjawals-MacBook-Pro.local>\\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi@openmrs.org>\",\"authorName\":\"Ujjawal Prabhat\",\"authorEmail\":\"UjjawalPrabhat1@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"f72aa14ce03ec28258c0acbe4507ac100b6fe8db\",\"date\":\"2026-08-27T19:33:55-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2703)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"7a2ccf502f6f557aa2628dee2371b2e70f8be5e3\",\"date\":\"2026-08-27T18:52:46+08:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-5760: Rework Service Queues dashboard to match design (#2615)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) O3-5760: Rework Service Queues dashboard to match design\\n\\n* (fix) e2e tests\\n\\n* (fix) Address review feedback on queues dashboard rework\\n\\n* (fix) Address review on queues dashboard rework\\n\\n* (fix) Address review feedback on queues dashboard rework\\n\\n- Bound the average wait time to entries started today and render '--'\\n  instead of 'NaN mins' when the backend has no completed waits to average\\n- Surface loading and error states in the Attending section so a failed\\n  request is no longer indistinguishable from nobody being attended\\n- Cap the Attending cards at three behind a 'View all' toggle and say\\n  'No one is being attended' explicitly when the list is empty\\n- Exclude Cancelled/Completed/Missed appointments from the expected\\n  appointments count and tab\\n- Translate appointment statuses, use a single interpolated key for the\\n  waiting list tab label, and use the framework age() helper so infants\\n  no longer render as '0 years old'\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5760: Address second round of review feedback on queues dashboard\\n\\nAdds concepts.waitingStatusConceptUuid so the waiting list, its tab count and\\nthe \\\"Waiting\\\" metric stop overloading defaultStatusConceptUuid, which only\\ndescribes the status a newly created queue entry starts in. All three read the\\nnew config, so the count cannot disagree with the rows beneath it.\\n\\n- Count the waiting list via queue-entry-metrics instead of paging through\\n  every entry. useQueueEntriesMetrics now reports isLoading and error so the\\n  tab label shows no momentary \\\"(0)\\\" before the request settles.\\n- Drop useServiceMetricsCount: it hardcoded status=Waiting as a concept name\\n  and has no remaining callers.\\n- Send forDate as an ISO 8601 string. The appointments module's DateUtil does\\n  not parse a ZZ numeric offset. The test now asserts the value, not the path.\\n- Show the selected service in the header even when the location is \\\"All\\\",\\n  since the modal permits that combination, and reset the service when the\\n  default location resolves, as services are scoped to a location.\\n- Look the expected-appointments name cell up through an id/patientUuid map\\n  rather than scanning every row on each render.\\n- Guard the service sort against a missing display, order attending-patients\\n  imports components before hooks, and drop an unused @carbon/type import.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5760: Trim the waitingStatusConceptUuid description\\n\\nIts contrast with defaultStatusConceptUuid belongs in review, not in the\\nconfig reference that implementers read.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5760: Scope the wait-time metric and Call action to the waiting status\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5760: Remove the appointments features from the dashboard\\n\\nThe Expected appointments tab and Appointments today card only match\\nappointments whose location equals the selected queue location exactly,\\nand the alternative leaks other locations' appointments. Dropping both\\nuntil location tagging is settled.\\n\\nAlso formats Avg. wait time like the Wait time column, and shows --\\nwhen the backend has nothing to average.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5760: Round the average wait time before guarding on it\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5760: Send the wait-time window as UTC\\n\\nThe queue module parses startedOnOrAfter with a zone-less\\nSimpleDateFormat, so browser-local midnight was read in the server's\\ntimezone and hid everything queued before the client's offset elapsed.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5760: Restructure the Attending card details\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5760: Move the service and priority into a card footer\\n\\nSeparates them from the demographics with a rule, service left and pill\\nright, per design review. The card element is now the link itself rather\\nthan a wrapper around one.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5760: Count the entries a search leaves in the waiting list heading\\n\\n`totalCount` is the server's count of every waiting entry, so the heading kept\\nreporting the full list while the table showed only the search results.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5760: Send the metrics window as an unambiguous instant\\n\\nThe queue module could not parse a timezone offset, so browser-local midnight\\nwas being converted to UTC and sent zone-less — correct only because servers\\nusually run in UTC. openmrs-module-queue now parses REST date parameters with\\nConversionUtil, so send an ISO-8601 instant and let the server resolve it.\\n\\nRequires queue module 3.1.0 or later.\\n\\n* (chore) Require queue module 3.1.0 for queue-entry-metrics\\n\\nThe average wait time card sends `startedOnOrAfter` as an ISO-8601 instant,\\nwhich only queue 3.1.0 onwards parses, so declare that in the backend\\ndependencies instead of noting it in a code comment. The `-0` prerelease\\nfloor keeps SNAPSHOT builds valid for testing.\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Ujjawal Prabhat <ujjawal@Ujjawals-MacBook-Pro.local>\\nCo-authored-by: jwnasambu <33891016+jwnasambu@users.noreply.github.com>\\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi@openmrs.org>\",\"authorName\":\"Ujjawal Prabhat\",\"authorEmail\":\"UjjawalPrabhat1@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"f2021aec08a29c7380aa08f74ac8af32cb27ca68\",\"date\":\"2026-08-26T17:14:11-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2700)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"2005c4e5e0b75fd20bc6ef97477dff378ea47cfa\",\"date\":\"2026-08-26T21:07:26+08:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-5765: Remove manual clear queue entries button (#2632)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ujjawal Prabhat\",\"authorEmail\":\"UjjawalPrabhat1@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"8738f2fd169e6901c17079d0e5d318e7d2ea7508\",\"date\":\"2026-08-13T16:33:58-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2677)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"88a3958024123fe1223a94c91af0675f34d621f8\",\"date\":\"2026-08-10T23:11:53+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Adopt @openmrs/eslint-config and ESLint 9 (#2664)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (chore) Adopt @openmrs/eslint-config and ESLint 9\\n\\nLint config moves to a flat eslint.config.mjs that spreads\\n@openmrs/eslint-config 2.0.0, replacing the root .eslintrc, the five\\npackage-level .eslintrc files, and .eslintignore. The seven ESLint plugin\\ndev dependencies the shared config provides are dropped, eslint moves from\\nthe end-of-life 8.57 line to ^9.39.0, and the --ext flag goes away since flat\\nconfig makes it redundant.\\n\\nRules this repo enforces beyond the shared defaults are kept in overlays:\\neqeqeq, the three ban-types successors that typescript-eslint's recommended\\npreset enables and the shared config turns off, and\\nreact-hooks/exhaustive-deps as a warning. Five packages enforced\\nno-explicit-any through their own .eslintrc, which ESLint 9 would ignore,\\nso that is now a path-scoped overlay covering the same five. Comparing the\\neffective rule set before and after on the same file, nothing this repo\\nenforced is lost, and both configurations report no findings over the same\\n680 files.\\n\\nThere are four kinds of fallout from the plugin versions the shared config\\npins.\\n\\neslint-plugin-react-hooks moves from 4.6 to 7.1, which recognizes React's\\nuse() hook. Playwright fixtures receive a callback named use and call it,\\nso the rule reports every fixture. rules-of-hooks is therefore off for\\ne2e, where React hook rules have no meaning.\\n\\neslint-plugin-playwright moves from 2.1 to 2.11. Eleven specs had a\\ntrailing top-level test.afterEach, which now warns. A top-level hook\\napplies to every test in the file wherever it sits, so moving it above the\\ntests changes nothing at runtime. Three page.selectOption calls become\\nlocator calls, which Playwright's own types point to as the replacement.\\nThe blank-line changes are autofixes.\\n\\nSeventeen eslint-disable comments in e2e/commands/encounter-operations.ts\\nnamed playwright rules. The playwright preset only applies to\\ne2e/**/*.spec.ts, so those comments never suppressed anything, and in flat\\nconfig a comment naming an unregistered rule is a hard error.\\n\\nTwo testing-library directives go away. The one in a test file is no longer\\nneeded, since that plugin moves from 6.5 to 7.16 and no longer reports\\nthere. The one in tools/test-utils.tsx named a rule that never applied to\\nit, since the preset only covers *.test.{ts,tsx}, so it is the same dead\\ncomment case as above.\\n\\n* (chore) Remove redundant cross-env wrappers\\n\\nThe lint scripts do not set environment variables, so they can invoke ESLint directly. Remove the unused root dependency and refresh the lockfile.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"4ab45c348ea730a9138c03bd72f7d01de93e3006\",\"date\":\"2026-08-08T16:31:20-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2662)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"}],\"totalCount\":94}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9999fda3-c5b6-4bd1-9a7c-3dae82c01922","uuid":"0e1d352a-fc32-4a3c-945d-94c4ebed60c5","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:18:17.388Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"b46bb56449a768d9ffb652006aa5eea2a8960c08\",\"date\":\"2026-08-28T18:08:3