{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Md73HzYBopVkfFEyvFEhVa","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"b4fa6bf0cb6141b90b1737507868ebe222cf9bba\",\"date\":\"2026-08-05T16:50:24-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2660)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"1af0d22714f5c85e3da513226acdb89d11bd1ac7\",\"date\":\"2026-08-04T16:52:53-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2655)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"9a9bd207717ecc2e1f551cafcc389cc1fa8ea40c\",\"date\":\"2026-08-03T16:49:49-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2653)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"ef2db8daa43241206aa85622ee9bf304928919bc\",\"date\":\"2026-07-31T16:47:55-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2650)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"3ebf29fd6a764a0b353cc7377b6a58ddcb9a3543\",\"date\":\"2026-08-01T01:52:31+08:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5681: Queue-screen widget polls regardless of user activity (#2564)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ujjawal Prabhat\",\"authorEmail\":\"UjjawalPrabhat1@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"2a05d2f532ff2713513d91ed56aafde26957a27e\",\"date\":\"2026-07-31T16:11:14+08:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-5769: Combine the Move and Transition row actions into one (#2611)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) O3-5769: Combine the Move and Transition row actions into one\\n\\n* (feat) Rename move confirmation strings and add status/priority tests\\n\\n* (fix) Keep the legacy transition action working\\n\\n* (fix) Address review feedback on the combined move action\\n\\n- Use neutral \\\"Queue entry updated\\\" copy for the submit notifications, since\\n  the modal now covers queue, status, and priority changes.\\n- Don't repeat a button action in the overflow menu when a deprecated action\\n  resolves to one already declared as a button (buttons: ['move'] with\\n  overflowMenu: ['transition'] rendered Move twice).\\n- Assert that the new priority reaches transitionQueueEntry in the\\n  priority-only test.\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: jwnasambu <33891016+jwnasambu@users.noreply.github.com>\\nCo-authored-by: Ujjawal Prabhat <ujjawal@Ujjawals-MacBook-Pro.local>\\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi@openmrs.org>\",\"authorName\":\"Ujjawal Prabhat\",\"authorEmail\":\"UjjawalPrabhat1@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"41835e897a10a266922a55adeb668632f52c90df\",\"date\":\"2026-07-31T01:55:21+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Remove nested anchor from the Service Queues admin card\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"The card wrapped ClickableTile in an outer anchor that carried the href.\\nClickableTile renders its own anchor, so this produced invalid nested\\nanchors and a dead tab stop: keyboard users would focus the outer link,\\nthen land on the tile itself, which had tabindex 0 but no href and did\\nnothing on Enter.\\n\\nThe href now lives on ClickableTile directly, matching how other admin\\ncards such as the Form Builder card are implemented. The cardLink\\nwrapper styles are no longer needed since there is no outer anchor left\\nto reset.\\n\",\"authorName\":\"denniskigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"b6315a9e5daf6d52ab2bda68f70a8f931e6a7b91\",\"date\":\"2026-07-30T16:47:22-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2647)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"0c695bcda73aa438cf88ba10cdddfe27ab22d590\",\"date\":\"2026-07-30T14:22:27+08:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-5761: List checked-in patients before search when adding to queue (#2633)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) O3-5761: List checked-in patients before search when adding to queue\\n\\n* (feat) O3-5761: Render checked-in patients with the patient banner\\n\\nReuse the framework patient-banner components for the checked-in patients\\nshortlist so its rows match patient-search results, and pass a mapped FHIR\\npatient to the selection callback instead of a bare uuid.\\n\\n- Add mapActiveVisitPatientToFhir to convert the REST visit patient into the\\n  minimal FHIR shape the banner components expect\\n- Widen the useActiveVisits custom representation accordingly and fetch all\\n  pages via useOpenmrsFetchAll so the list isn't truncated\\n- Drop the restrictToToday parameter; the server-side fromStartDate filter\\n  already scopes results to today\\n- Move the config gate to AddPatientToQueueButton and rename the property to\\n  showCheckedInPatientsBeforeSearch\\n- Add loading and error states, and cover the new behaviour with tests\\n\\n* (chore) O3-5761: Clarify that the checked-in patients list is location-scoped\\n\\nThe queue-entry exclusion is filtered by the selected queue location, but the\\ndoc comment and empty-state copy implied it covered any queue. Reword both to\\nmatch the actual scope.\\n\\n* (chore) O3-5761: Pin the location scope of the checked-in patients exclusion\\n\\nThe shortlist filters active visits against queue entries scoped to the selected location, which is deliberate: a patient can legitimately hold entries at several locations, and the backend only rejects a repeat entry in the same queue. Nothing asserted the criteria passed to useQueueEntries, so that scope could have drifted silently.\\n\\n* (chore) translation changes\\n\\n* (chore) O3-5761: Clarify that the checked-in patients shortlist is today-only\\n\\nThe docblock said the list shows patients \\\"with an active visit\\\", but\\nuseActiveVisits always sends fromStartDate=<today>, so an open visit that\\nstarted before today is excluded. Spell out the today-only scope.\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: NethmiRodrigo <nethmi.dilinika@gmail.com>\\nCo-authored-by: Ujjawal Prabhat <ujjawal@10-64-49-196.0200.binb.id.iosda.org>\\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi@openmrs.org>\",\"authorName\":\"Ujjawal Prabhat\",\"authorEmail\":\"UjjawalPrabhat1@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"171573ddff7840281d76268628e2684ed3be64d0\",\"date\":\"2026-07-29T18:47:10+08:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5693: Trim queue entry representation to what the table renders (#2583)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ujjawal Prabhat\",\"authorEmail\":\"UjjawalPrabhat1@gmail.com\"}],\"totalCount\":94}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9999fda3-c5b6-4bd1-9a7c-3dae82c01922","uuid":"c0812bc0-8296-4798-99a8-db63d03f7f47","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:18:23.008Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"b4fa6bf0cb6141b90b1737507868ebe222cf9bba\",\"date\":\"2026-08-05T16:50:24-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2660)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"1af0d22714f5c85e3da513226acdb89d11bd1ac7\",\"date\":\"2026-08-04T16:52:53-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2655)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"9a9bd207717ecc2e1f551cafcc389cc1fa8ea40c\",\"date\":\"2026-08-03T16:49:49-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2653)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"ef2db8daa43241206aa85622ee9bf304928919bc\",\"date\":\"2026-07-31T16:47:55-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2650)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"3ebf29fd6a764a0b353cc7377b6a58ddcb9a3543\",\"date\":\"2026-08-01T01:52:31+08:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5681: Queue-screen widget polls regardless of user activity (#2564)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ujjawal Prabhat\",\"authorEmail\":\"UjjawalPrabhat1@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"2a05d2f532ff2713513d91ed56aafde26957a27e\",\"date\":\"2026-07-31T16:11:14+08:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-5769: Combine the Move and Transition row actions into one (#2611)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) O3-5769: Combine the Move and Transition row actions into one\\n\\n* (feat) Rename move confirmation strings and add status/priority tests\\n\\n* (fix) Keep the legacy transition action working\\n\\n* (fix) Address review feedback on the combined move action\\n\\n- Use neutral \\\"Queue entry updated\\\" copy for the submit notifications, since\\n  the modal now covers queue, status, and priority changes.\\n- Don't repeat a button action in the overflow menu when a deprecated action\\n  resolves to one already declared as a button (buttons: ['move'] with\\n  overflowMenu: ['transition'] rendered Move twice).\\n- Assert that the new priority reaches transitionQueueEntry in the\\n  priority-only test.\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: jwnasambu <33891016+jwnasambu@users.noreply.github.com>\\nCo-authored-by: Ujjawal Prabhat <ujjawal@Ujjawals-MacBook-Pro.local>\\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi@openmrs.org>\",\"authorName\":\"Ujjawal Prabhat\",\"authorEmail\":\"UjjawalPrabhat1@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"41835e897a10a266922a55adeb668632f52c90df\",\"date\":\"2026-07-31T01:55:21+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Remove nested anchor from the Service Queues admin card\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"The card wrapped ClickableTile in an outer anchor that carried the href.\\nClickableTile renders its own anchor, so this produced invalid nested\\nanchors and a dead tab stop: keyboard users would focus the outer link,\\nthen land on the tile itself, which had tabindex 0 but no href and did\\nnothing on Enter.\\n\\nThe href now lives on ClickableTile directly, matching how other admin\\ncards such as the Form Builder card are implemented. The cardLink\\nwrapper styles are no longer needed since there is no outer anchor left\\nto reset.\\n\",\"authorName\":\"denniskigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"b6315a9e5daf6d52ab2bda68f70a8f931e6a7b91\",\"date\":\"2026-07-30T16:47:22-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#2647)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"0c695bcda73aa438cf88ba10cdddfe27ab22d590\",\"date\":\"2026-07-30T14:22:27+08:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-5761: List checked-in patients before search when adding to queue (#2633)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) O3-5761: List checked-in patients before search when adding to queue\\n\\n* (feat) O3-5761: Render checked-in patients with the patient banner\\n\\nReuse the framework patient-banner components for the checked-in patients\\nshortlist so its rows match patient-search results, and pass a mapped FHIR\\npatient to the selection callback instead of a bare uuid.\\n\\n- Add mapActiveVisitPatientToFhir to convert the REST visit patient into the\\n  minimal FHIR shape the banner components expect\\n- Widen the useActiveVisits custom representation accordingly and fetch all\\n  pages via useOpenmrsFetchAll so the list isn't truncated\\n- Drop the restrictToToday parameter; the server-side fromStartDate filter\\n  already scopes results to today\\n- Move the config gate to AddPatientToQueueButton and rename the property to\\n  showCheckedInPatientsBeforeSearch\\n- Add loading and error states, and cover the new behaviour with tests\\n\\n* (chore) O3-5761: Clarify that the checked-in patients list is location-scoped\\n\\nThe queue-entry exclusion is filtered by the selected queue location, but the\\ndoc comment and empty-state copy implied it covered any queue. Reword both to\\nmatch the actual scope.\\n\\n* (chore) O3-5761: Pin the location scope of the checked-in patients exclusion\\n\\nThe shortlist filters active visits against queue entries scoped to the selected location, which is deliberate: a patient can legitimately hold entries at several locations, and the backend only rejects a repeat entry in the same queue. Nothing asserted the criteria passed to useQueueEntries, so that scope could have drifted silently.\\n\\n* (chore) translation changes\\n\\n* (chore) O3-5761: Clarify that the checked-in patients shortlist is today-only\\n\\nThe docblock said the list shows patients \\\"with an active visit\\\", but\\nuseActiveVisits always sends fromStartDate=<today>, so an open visit that\\nstarted before today is excluded. Spell out the today-only scope.\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: NethmiRodrigo <nethmi.dilinika@gmail.com>\\nCo-authored-by: Ujjawal Prabhat <ujjawal@10-64-49-196.0200.binb.id.iosda.org>\\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi@openmrs.org>\",\"authorName\":\"Ujjawal Prabhat\",\"authorEmail\":\"UjjawalPrabhat1@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"171573ddff7840281d76268628e2684ed3be64d0\",\"date\":\"2026-07-29T18:47:10+08:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5693: Trim queue entry representation to what the table renders (#2583)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ujjawal Prabhat\",\"authorEmail\":\"UjjawalPrabhat1@gmail.com\"}],\"totalCount\":94}"}],"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Md73HzYBopVkfFEyvFEhVa","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
